# rm483, the sergeant's spare bowl (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm483
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_bettany_nailley
written_by codex
title the sergeant's spare bowl
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=guard
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk counts_kindnesses_by_the_empty_bowls_on_a_pantry_shelf
likes pickled_herring stars full_larder first_snow
dislikes early_bells flies
fears a_missing_wolf_reduced_to_a_wharf_entry
hopes a_watch_that_remembers_the_unheard
topics work +0.6 home +0.5 food +0.4 memories +0.4
styles comfort=warm gossip=careful refuse=gentle tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# counts debts by the empty places on a pantry shelf and gives a shy voice the same patient hearing as a loud one.

words
oath! = Rattle my spare bowl | Chalk the wrong star
saying! = A debt remembers which bowl came back | Leave the last shelf open for a kindness
bowl = a shallow brown bowl | a patched tin bowl
shelf = a dry pantry shelf | a high board
jar = a jar of herring | a salt crock
lid = a glazed lid | a loose wood cover
tally = a little debt mark | a double stroke
star = a speck of white | a fixed point
snow = the pale first fall | a quiet scattering
pledge = a word owed | a remembered promise
bell = an impertinent bell | an early iron call
fly = a drowsy fly | a brazen little speck
spoon = a plain serving spoon | a deep horn spoon
door = the half-shut door | a sheltered door
purse = an exact account | a tidy count
step = a clear doorstep | a grey flag
cloth = the salt cloth | a white pot cloth
lamp = the low lamp | a steady lamp
badge = the mark of duty | a shoulder badge
gutter = the street drain | a broad gutter

any
opinion @1 dole for 3 : A ladle scraping an empty pot sounds very different to a wolf whose bowl is still empty.
opinion @1 watch for 1 : The quiet voice has as much right to finish speaking as the loud one. I want a watch that hears both.
opinion @1 houses against 3 : A tally of returned cargo cannot tell me that every place at a wharf supper was filled again.
opinion @1 church for 1 : A decent service leaves space to be sore without making an exhibit of the sorrow.
opinion @1 sump for 2 [self.quarter=sump] : We can set a spare bowl down here without first holding a meeting over who is coming.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : A stranger needn't know which door to knock on for me to point out the latch.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : I like a seller who turns the sum to face the payer.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : A street can sound cheerful without having to sound orderly at every instant.
opinion @1 times against 2 [world.times=lean|hard] : Too many wolves remember exactly what they owe because the cupboard has space for little else.

grown
line @1 greet : Come round and sit. I'll shift along. | Good to see you. I've a minute free.
line @1 greet.return : Back again. I'd hoped you might be.
line @1 again.open : Back before the spare bowl's cold.
line @1 farewell : Safe home to a light you know. | Keep a little ease in your shoulders on the way.
line @1 farewell.return : A decent doorway at your own journey's end.
line @1 react.news : Let me hear it where the account began. | Speak until you've said your piece.
line @1 react.news.new : First mark of that I've seen.
line @1 react.news.known : I remember the earlier telling very clearly.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'm leaving a gap beside that claim for what we haven't heard.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : I'd take the first watch beside that hurt.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : There's a bright place at table for such news.
line @1 ask.how : Anything you need to set down before you start?
line @1 answer.how : Steady. Whoever comes next gets both ears.
line @1 sympathise : Tell as much as you have breath for.
line @1 reassure : I've known courage come up quietly after a warm bite.
line @1 refuse : I have another wolf's time already in my keeping.
line @1 accept_decline : That answer can stand without my pushing at it.
line @1 preclose : I should pay the next bit of time where it's owed.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go finish the good thing you set out to do.
line @1 ack : Every piece of that account has landed.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : One quiet welcome before the louder bell.
line @3 greet [pair.band=strangers] : A fresh face has a full turn to speak here.
line @4 greet [here.time=night] : Welcome while there's a little lamp light left.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends] : I'd always keep some warm bench for that familiar voice.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Round here by the low light, there's a place!
line @1 thank : A favour like that goes on the shelf beside my own bowl.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I had the hour and you had a use for it.
line @1 give.advice : Start with what you actually saw. Give doubt its own bit of paper.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : A few voices are waiting, but no voice need rush its last word.
line @2 ask.how [pair.band=friends] : Have the low streets been treating your feet kindly?
scene exchange1
when topic=work self.job=guard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wait till a witness finishes before I start my line. | I keep two stools if I can.
b : Afraid of missing a word? | Why a second?
a : Afraid I'll write the ending I expected. | A wolf coming in shaken needn't stand while I sit.

scene exchange2
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember kindnesses as empty bowls waiting on a shelf. | My old tallies have one line I never closed.
b : Whose goes first? | Is something still owed on it?
a : The one that can go back full today. | Not in coin. A wolf went missing off the wharf once, and no sum fills that.

scene exchange3
when topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Herring needs a deep dish if you're going to pass it round. | I take the narrow end for myself when I share.
b : Is it lively in the brine? | Why?
a : A very dead fish can still salt three innocent cuffs. | It comes out first. No kindness in keeping the dinner waiting.

scene exchange4
when topic=pastimes self.likes=stars
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I name a kindness to myself when a star first shows. | On clear nights I walk home slowly with my muzzle tipped up.
b : Enough stars for all of them? | Even in the cold?
a : Often well past bedtime before I'm done. | The cold usually turns me round before the stars run out.

scene exchange5
when topic=home self.likes=full_larder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A stocked pantry sounds quiet when a jar goes down. | I keep one shelf end vacant.
b : Quiet how? | Expecting more food?
a : A close packed shelf leaves little space for rattling. | Expecting someone's hands to be full on arrival.

scene exchange6
when topic=season self.likes=first_snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : First snow makes a distinct line under every lamp. | I let one flake settle on my dark cuff.
b : Are you following footprints? | Keeping account of winter?
a : I'm enjoying a street before it needs anything of me. | The opening entry. It disappears as soon as I move.

scene exchange7
when topic=day self.dislikes=early_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An early bell wakes every debt I've ever remembered. | I'd happily miss the first clang of the morning.
b : All needing answers at once? | What about the second?
a : All of them, and none willing to wait its turn. | By then I've admitted there's a morning.

scene exchange8
when topic=animals self.dislikes=flies
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A fly can find my herring through a lid and a towel. | I turn an empty bowl over the jar before I sit down.
b : A gifted investigator? | Does that keep them off?
a : One with no regard at all for whose supper it is. | Mostly. One always finds the chip in the rim.

scene exchange9
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave a quiet space in a blessing for a missing voice. | I give thanks before a jar comes off the high shelf.
b : Does it need a name? | Why before?
a : I know the one I mean. The room can be spared the particulars. | So I can lift with both paws and a clear head.

scene exchange10
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd trust #self.friend# with a sore account still unfinished. | I'd keep a seat facing the stars for a friend.
b : Which favour would repay it? | And where would you sit?
a : A little patience while I find the proper end. | Facing the friend. I've seen the stars before.

scene exchange11
when topic=work self.role=guard self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I give the quiet visitor time to get past the first word. | I keep the writing surface clear of my lunch.
b : Does that delay the room? | For appearances?
a : It saves bringing the whole matter round a second time. | So nobody feels like a nuisance who's interrupted my meal.

scene exchange12
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The report says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. My hearing ends there. | Talk can reach every doorstep before the first witness has dried off.
b : No judgement? | Would you hurry the witness?
a : A report and a finding deserve separate shelves. | I'd fetch a cloth. Then I'd listen.

scene exchange13
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In lean weeks I keep closer count of returned bowls. | Dear food brings a different pause to questions about home.
b : Who forgot to pay? | Do you press for more?
a : Who's had to manage without enough. That's the count I want. | Not in the street. I'll find somewhere private first.

scene exchange14
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like coming home along the unlit edge of the street. | I can count my route by the smells of supper.
b : A gloomy walk? | Which one means home?
a : Far better for the stars than the side with windows. | The vinegar at the last turn has a particularly familiar bite.

scene exchange15
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want mine to be a voice that has time left after everybody else is heard. | I'd like a pantry door that could swing outward to a whole street.
b : A large ambition? | Wouldn't you run bare?
a : Big enough that I'm still finding better ways to work. | I'd watch what's brought in as well as the going out.

scene exchange16
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The Sump remembers a favour longer than a mark on a door. | I see the wharf from the headland and sometimes stop walking.
b : Because the rain washes the mark? | Afraid of the drop?
a : Because a pot comes back to the doorstep when the ink's long gone. | Remembering what's owed to wolves working below.

scene exchange17
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I count a bill aloud if the payer asks. | A fair bowlful ought to come at the figure marked.
b : Only then? | Even when the board's nearly bare?
a : Some sums are as private as a kitchen after supper. | Especially then. Hunger has already raised the price.

scene exchange18
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I loosen my coat when my shoulders feel higher than my ears. | A tired voice often goes very small at its most important word.
b : Hard day? | Do you ask for it again?
a : Sometimes just a crowded one. I make space deliberately. | I lean closer first. A little less effort may be enough.

scene exchange19
when topic=work self.job=guard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A question should fit whoever must supply its answer. | One good breath precedes my refusing a request.
b : Do you change the facts? | Looking for a gentler refusal?
a : I change the words until the facts can be told without guessing my meaning. | Checking whether the answer really has to be no.

scene exchange20
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A newcomer with a soaked bundle gets my driest peg. | I ask how a stranger says a name.
b : Before asking business? | Why not read it?
a : A free paw is worth a surprising amount in an unfamiliar room. | Letters represent a voice. They aren't entitled to correct it.

scene exchange21
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't bring my work to the supper table. | My pantry light reaches the threshold.
b : Not even a little of it? | For seeing late visitors?
a : Not a scrap. The table stays free of obligations long enough to eat. | For letting them see that a foot inside is welcome.

scene exchange22
when topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like fish in vinegar best with a plain heel of bread. | I rinse the serving fork after each jar.
b : Does the bread dull it? | Even for more herring?
a : It lets the second taste start again. | A different jar might have a different idea about seasoning.

scene exchange23
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember a kindness in its giver's voice. | A wharf can be busy enough to hide a very empty place.
b : What if a voice changes? | Busy how?
a : Then the kindness has two ways to call me back. | Crowds at the cranes all day. Come nightfall you notice who isn't at supper.

scene exchange24
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The hard part of winter isn't always cold. | In spring I can shift the lamp higher.
b : What else? | Because it's light later?
a : The distance from one warm door to the next ready meal. | So the returning crew can see the light from farther along the walk.

scene exchange25
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I count the pantry spoons back before I sleep. | I take my first mouthful sitting if there's a stool.
b : Fear for the silver? | Even in a hurry?
a : They're horn. I want to know breakfast can start without a search. | Particularly in a hurry. It sets the pace for the next mouthful.

scene exchange26
when topic=pastimes self.likes=stars
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I watch a bright star through a little notch in the roofline. | A cloudy night makes me work at remembering the shapes.
b : What if it moves? | Can you really remember them all?
a : I enjoy the moment it crosses a place I recognise. | No. That's why a clear night remains a gift.

scene exchange27
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Rain makes my public coat too heavy for the same peg as my meal bag. | I put the damp cloth on a rail where the air can pass.
b : Does the peg sag? | Not beside the jar?
a : Eventually. Heavy things ought to have their weight acknowledged. | Herring's plenty old enough to supply its own flavour.

scene exchange28
when topic=work self.role=guard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A calm room makes it easier to hear disagreement clearly. | I repeat a difficult name before my pen goes near it.
b : Do you dislike disagreement? | For the spelling?
a : I dislike missing what sets one account apart from another. | For the wolf who had to come and give it.

scene exchange29
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I would like to give out a watch tally consisting entirely of wolves safely home. | I'd put the stars on the cover of my private book.
b : Too simple for a report? | Why leave the pages plain?
a : No little achievement, getting a whole street home. | The things inside are bright enough to stand alone.

scene exchange30
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A little coin ought to make its whole sound in the pan. | I pay my debt in the form in which it's owed.
b : Can you hear how much? | Always coin?
a : I can hear that somebody has emptied a purse very carefully. | Time, a clean bowl, a turn with a heavy basket. Coppers can't do every job.

story tale1 [topic=memories]
  : A visitor returned a soup bowl with a herring laid neatly inside. I knew the bowl by its blue rim. The fish was a very agreeable surprise.
  : I served the herring at supper and set the empty bowl back in its old place.
  b : Was the debt settled?
  : The bowl certainly was. The unexpected kindness wanted a fresh mark all to itself.

story tale2 [topic=work self.job=guard]
  : I once gave a witness a beautifully clean slate for a sketch. The first mark was a square in the corner, apparently of enormous significance.
  : It turned out to represent the window we were standing beside.
  b : What did the window tell you?
  : Where the witness had stood when the matter began. The first mark which looked unnecessary was what let the whole account make sense.

story tale3 [topic=pastimes self.likes=stars]
  : I tried laying out the headland stars with little bowls on a table. The largest star wanted a much larger vessel than I owned.
  : I used the bread cloth folded round an upturned pot.
  b : Did it make a convincing sky?
  : Only till dinner. We ate most of the constellation and went outdoors for the original.

story tale4 [topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring]
  : I took vinegar for a dull bowl and put salt in before tasting it. The first mouthful did a rather impressive job of finding every corner of my muzzle.
  : I added bread in quiet, considered stages.
  b : Did the salt ever admit defeat?
  : I shared the broth between three bowls before it did. There's a reason I like hearing a matter before putting more into it.

story tale5 [topic=season self.likes=first_snow]
  : I found the mark of a little bowl in the first snow on the sill. A perfect circle without a single flake in the middle.
  : I had forgotten moving my spare bowl indoors just after the snow began.
  b : Did it find its old circle again?
  : I kept the circle clear for a while. Even an absent thing can have a shape worth noticing.

rule @call1
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=guard
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Give the quiet account a chance to finish. | Both ears open before the chalk goes down.

rule @call2
when concept=bark working=yes self.role=guard
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Dry stool for a caller with a wet coat. | Keep the writing corner clear for the next report.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One bright star above the pantry light. | The late route has its own patient glimmer.

rule @call4
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The bell needn't claim every ear all at once. | A dry cuff before the first entry.

rule @call5
when concept=bark self.dislikes=flies
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That jar already has all the company it needs. | Cover down till the fork's ready.

rule @call6
when concept=bark self.likes=full_larder
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A little space among the full pots for a visitor's parcel. | That's a comfortable sound off the pantry shelf.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Say what brings you in without hurrying the first part.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I remember more than a name against an entry.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Late business and early worry can share the lamp for a minute.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : You're entitled to hear what I'm asking and why.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=guard] : I serve the Watch. The rank on the coat hasn't taken away the duty of listening to the last wolf in line.
dlg @2 resident.job : I keep account of what I've promised and make room for the next voice.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : The public report that came to me is #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : The word reported was #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's a matter of hearing rather than witnessing.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Come away with the account clearer and the walk a little lighter.
dlg @1 watch.hub [here.wanted=yes] : There's a Watch matter standing against you. The sum entered is #here.fine# pennies. You can ask me about it.
dlg @2 watch.hub [here.wanted=no on_watch=yes] : I'm on duty and ready to hear what you need from the Watch.
dlg @3 watch.hub [here.wanted=no on_watch=no] : I'm off watch. I can give an ordinary question an ordinary hearing.
dlg @1 watch.crime [here.witnessed=0] : Tell me in your own words what you saw. I won't put a line down before you start.
dlg @1 watch.reported [topic.reported=yes] : Your report's entered. The particulars you gave are part of the record.
dlg @1 watch.fine [here.wanted=no] : Your account with the Watch stands clear. That's a short and very decent entry.
dlg @2 watch.fine [here.wanted=yes] : The Watch account currently records #here.fine# pennies against you.
dlg @1 watch.bye : Walk out in good order and find a quiet roof.
graft resident.hub
choice How do you remember every little favour? -> return_bowl
node return_bowl
say I give each one an empty place in my mind. When I reach for an imaginary bowl, I can tell quite precisely who should get the next warm helping.
free
choice Must it be repaid in food? -> return_bowl_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node return_bowl_again
say Not at all. Somebody once gave me time when time was what I lacked. I'd like to return the same courtesy to somebody still gathering words.
choice Leave a place for the next caller. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft watch.hub
choice How does a quiet witness get heard? [self.job=guard] -> quiet_hearing
node quiet_hearing
say Turn the seat towards the light and give the voice time. Once the first bit comes out, it is often quite clear what question ought to follow.
free
choice Do you record a guess? -> quiet_hearing_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node quiet_hearing_again
say As a guess, expressly. Ink should not change an uncertain word into a very confident one.
choice Let's return to the Watch business. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
